Z||000005||mrfixit58||03-16-2000||04:57 PM||||DXR_DAD,<P>Well, as it turned out the fabric was just too rotten. The seat were not torn but had mildew spots. I took chance when I bought them but for the $20 for the pair, it was worth the shot. I only tried to machine wash one seat bottom so I still have one good (maybe) seat back.<P>I found a local upholster shop that can color match (if not exact material) the tan material and brown vinyl. And, when they make the seat covers they will sew the "Fiero" patch on the seat backs all for around $200. They cam highly recommended.<P>So, if I can't find a good used set, I will probably go that route. Or, with Mr. Mike's. But we'll cross that bridge when we get there. I'm still a ways away from getting her on the road.<P>Thanks again for the help,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||9
